nts when candidates got stuck.","preparationMaterials":"Striver's A2Z/455 DSA sheet, LeetCode contests, GeeksforGeeks for CS fundamentals (OOPs, DBMS, OS), and reading up on Visa before the interview.","suggestions":"Start DSA preparation early (2-3 months minimum). Be genuine and communicate your thought process clearly, even when unsure of the answer.","sourcePage":310},{"id":"wells-fargo-program-associate-technology-2026-27","company":"Wells Fargo","profile":"Program Associate - Technology","location":"Bangalore, Hyderabad, Chennai","year":"2026-27","eligibleAllBranches":true,"eligibleBranches":[],"cgpa":{"status":"known","min":7.5},"compensation":{"max_ctc_lpa":35.0},"offers":3,"test":null,"gd":"No GD.","interviewRounds":null,"roleCategories":["Other"],"jobDescription":"Click here to view Job Description","shortlistingProcess":"","testAndInterview":"Written test with 3 questions covering System Design (e.g. a regex-based problem), DSA (medium-hard), and SQL (medium). 3 rounds (2 technical + 1 HR/behavioural), generally offline with one to two panelists. Round 1 needs broad CS fundamentals and DSA knowledge; Round 2 focuses on software-life-cycle understanding and applying concepts like the CAP theorem to real client scenarios - a client-centric mindset is valued. Interviewers were described as kind and approachable. No case-study or GD rounds.","preparationMaterials":"Striver's A2Z DSA sheet, LeetCode 50 for SQL, coursework in DBMS/Operating Systems, and YouTube resources for core CS concepts; some also referenced Fundamentals of Data Engineering and ML/Transformer-architecture material.","suggestions":"Build a strong, detailed resume and be well-versed in CS fundamentals alongside DSA - this combination gives a clear edge over other candidates.","sourcePage":314},{"id":"wipro-enterprises-pvt-ltd-graduate-engineer-trainee-get-2026-27","company":"Wipro Enterprises Pvt Ltd","profile":"Graduate Engineer Trainee (GET)","location":"Hindupur, Peenya, Chennai, or Jaipu